## Control {{controlId}}: Implement Cryptographic Mechanisms to Prevent Unauthorized Disclosure of CUI During Transmission

**Implementation Status:** {{status}}

This organization implements cryptographic protections for CUI during transmission within the {{tenantName}} M365 GCC High tenant through TLS enforcement, Exchange Online transport rules, and encrypted communication channels managed by {{variables.systemAdministrator}}.

{{#if transportConfigured}}
**Transport Layer Security:**
Exchange Online transport encryption enforces **{{tlsVersion}}** for all email communications containing CUI. {{#if enforceEncryption}}Encryption is mandatory for all outbound connections.{{/if}} {{#if requireTLS}}TLS is required for partner organization mail flow connectors.{{/if}}

All M365 GCC High services enforce FIPS 140-2 validated cryptographic modules for data in transit:
- **Exchange Online:** TLS {{tlsVersion}} for SMTP, IMAP, and ActiveSync connections
- **SharePoint Online / OneDrive:** HTTPS (TLS {{tlsVersion}}) for all file transfers
- **Teams:** SRTP for media and TLS {{tlsVersion}} for signaling
{{else}}
Transport encryption configuration has not been confirmed. CUI in transit may not be cryptographically protected to FIPS 140-2 standards.
{{/if}}

**Responsible Party:** {{variables.systemAdministrator}}

**Verification Method:** Examine Exchange Online transport rules, TLS configuration settings, mail flow connector encryption requirements, and FIPS 140-2 validation certificates.

